  "contentHtml": "<p>1. <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0047272726001714\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tax land more heavily than structures</a>.</p>\n<p>2. “<a href=\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/british-journal-of-political-science/article/equality-positions-and-policies-of-governments-19702020-how-egalitarian-parties-evoke-equality-while-evading-real-redistribution/6E39434BFECCF3B4B967F83A63798C3F\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Our findings suggest that equality-oriented governments adopt an approach that insures the middle, buffers the poor, but spares the rich. The result is a rhetorical commitment to equality that eschews its most redistributive instrument(s).</a>”</p>\n<p>3. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qhlySf8k0i0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Francesco Cabella conversation with (an older) Victor Niederhoffer</a>.</p>\n<p>4. <a href=\"https://unityhomes.co.ke/silver-hill/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">New homes in Tatu City, Kenya</a>.</p>\n<p>5. <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/08/us/bill-goichberg-dead.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bill Goichberg, RIP</a> (NYT).&nbsp; America’s greatest chess organizer, he was always very nice and encouraging to me.</p>\n<p>6. <a href=\"https://www.programmablemutter.com/p/john-crowley-has-died?r=1g4uc&amp;utm_medium=ios&amp;triedRedirect=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">John Crowley, RIP</a>.</p>\n<p>7. <a href=\"https://jaredhenderson.substack.com/p/the-literacy-crisis-more-than-you?r=1g4uc&amp;utm_medium=ios&amp;triedRedirect=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Data on literacy and reading</a>.</p>",
